# Chart Fix — Blast Radius

When fixing or changing chart engine code, local correctness is not enough. Shared state in `createChart.ts` (camera, dirty flags, layer buffers, crosshair, interaction) means one fix often regresses neighbors.

## Before editing
1. Name the **target behavior** and the **shared state** it touches (VisibleRange, dirty flags, layer buffers, coords/scales, crosshair, follow mode).
2. List **blast-radius neighbors** that share that state (series / indicators / overlay paint, pan-zoom, follow, multi-pane, touch).
3. Prefer the smallest vertical diff. No “while we’re here” refactors in `createChart.ts`.

## Do not break (verify every chart fix)
- Layer invalidate still correct: series | indicators | overlay
- Mid-drag / overlay-only paint does **not** force a full series rebuild
- Pan, wheel zoom, axis drag, follow mode, and camera preserve still work
- Crosshair snap / OHLC readout still align with logical index
- Touch / pointer paths still work (~390px mental check)
- Perf contract untouched: dirty + rAF only; viewport buffer ≤ `MAX_BARS_IN_MEMORY`

## After editing
1. Run related tests under `src/chart/__tests__/` (not only the new/changed file).
2. If a neighbor broke in this session, add a **regression test** at the seam before finishing.
3. In the reply: state what was fixed, what blast radius was checked, and any residual risk.

## Examples
```text
❌ BAD: “Fixed crosshair snap” (only touched crosshair.ts, no neighbor check)

✅ GOOD: “Fixed crosshair snap in crosshair.ts. Did not change series/indicator
paint paths. Checked layer invalidate + pan/zoom/follow. Ran chart tests.”
```
